room      law_2
kind      equation
import    Newton, Principia, Andrew Motte trans., 1729 (Wikisource); Axioms, or Laws of Motion, Law II.
caption   Law II --- The alteration of motion is ever proportional to the motive force impressed; and is made in the direction of the right line in which that force is impressed.
final     2

station 1
  ceiling   eq_prop :: \Delta p \propto F
  gloss   The alteration of motion scales exactly with the impressed force.
  color   motion #C21807
  color   force #1B5E9C
  color   plain #000000
  panel
    term    motion  $\Delta(\text{motion})$  heart stabilo=#C21807
    term    plain   $\;\propto\;$
    term    force   $F$
    layout  $\{motion|\Delta(\text{motion})\} \;\propto\; \{force|F\}$
  text
    {motion|The alteration of motion} is ever proportional to the {force|motive force impress'd}: "if any {force|force} generates a {motion|motion}, a double {force|force} will generate double the {motion|motion}," and a triple {force|force} triple the {motion|motion}. This holds whether the {force|force} be impress'd altogether and at once, or gradually and successively. The exact scaling is the heart of the law --- $\{motion|\Delta(\text{motion})\} \propto \{force|F\}$ --- the seed from which $F = ma$ grows.

station 2
  ceiling   eq_dir :: \Delta p \parallel F
  gloss   The change of motion lies along the same right line as the force.
  color   line #C21807
  color   force #1B5E9C
  color   old #6A1B9A
  color   plain #000000
  panel
    term    line   $\Delta(\text{motion})$  heart stabilo=#C21807
    term    plain  $\;\parallel\;$
    term    force  $F$
    layout  $\{line|\Delta(\text{motion})\} \;\parallel\; \{force|F\}$
  text
    The {line|alteration is made in the direction of the right line} in which that {force|force} is impress'd --- {line|always directed the same way} with the generating {force|force}. If the body {old|moved before}, this new {line|motion} is added to or subducted from the {old|former motion}, according as they directly conspire or are directly contrary. When they are {line|obliquely joyned}, the {force|force} and the {old|prior motion} compound by the parallelogram rule, so as to produce a new {line|motion compounded from the determination of both} --- hence $\{line|\Delta(\text{motion})\} \parallel \{force|F\}$.
